std::event_loop::revoke or, as a method, receiver.revoke(...).

== DESCRIPTION
Revoke REG: no handler invocation after this one. Its queued events are
discarded, a wake already queued for a task becomes Wake::Revoked when the
task is dispatched, records still in flight are dropped as stale, and every
waiter is made ready with Wake::Revoked, in the order they waited. Running
code is not undone and no task is cancelled. True when REG was live (or a
spent one-shot timer); revoking twice, or a stale copy, does nothing
(false). An owned registration is revoked by its Owner only (release):
revoking it through its Reg does nothing (false).

