Path is an ordinary eager trait (TRAITS.md): a value of any concrete path
type whose own namespace implements `concat` and `text` may enter it, and a
function over Path is specialized per concrete type, so `path.concat` above
compiles to a direct call of the concrete type's own concat (for a
std::linux::path::LinuxPath, std::linux::path::concat), with no wrapper or
dispatch. The concrete types live with their platforms --
std::linux::path::LinuxPath, a future Windows path -- and this namespace
knows none of them.

