== DESCRIPTION
uri_query_value?(value) decides whether VALUE is safe to embed as a URI
query value, and when true proves it a UriQueryValue (REFINEMENT-
VALUES.md): every UTF-8 byte is an RFC 3986 unreserved character
(is_unreserved) or begins a percent-encoded triplet "%XX" of two uppercase
hexadecimal digits -- exactly the alphabet uri_escape_text writes, so every
string it produces passes. The refinement used to be "opaque": a value was a
UriQueryValue only when a trusted native had attached runtime evidence to it
(stdlib/web.tcl's uriEscape). Refinements carry no runtime evidence, so the
proposition is now this structural check, owned and defined here.

